## Original Content
Thirty people died in Guinea's capital Conakry on Sunday when a mound of rubbish in a landfill collapsed before dawn onto neighboring homes following heavy rains, the government said.

## Summary
A landslide at a landfill in Conakry, Guinea, caused by heavy rains, killed 30 people when it buried neighboring homes before dawn on Sunday. The government reported the incident, emphasizing the disaster's impact.

## Key Points
- 30 people died in a landfill landslide in Conakry, Guinea.
- The collapse occurred following heavy rains.
- Neighboring homes were buried under rubbish.


